# Does a REGISTER seed change the path? 0x8C09C1F4 dispatches on r0
# (cmp/eq #N,r0 for N in {1,3,6,7,8,9,16}) and has no gate on a live global
# before that dispatch, so r0 alone must select a different arm.
# No `ram` lines at all - if coverage still differs between the two files,
# the register path works and the defect is isolated to the RAM path.
entry 0x8c048284 0x8c09c1f4
reg 0x8c048284 pr 0x8c048286
reg 0x8c048284 r0 0x00000001
